First, I need to recall what the term 'era' typically refers to in computer science. The term 'era' in the context of data structures might be related to the time period during which an element exists in a certain state. For example, in a stack, each element has an era when it's pushed and when it's popped. Alternatively, in some contexts, 'era' could refer to the version or generation of elements, like in generational garbage collection where each object has an era indicating when it was created.

